=== A. Last trading day: current practice vs Effective TBD ===
  current AM-settled index options (except planned VIX change): cease at the market close
    on the business day prior to expiration (usually a Thursday)
  current PM-settled options: cease at 4:00 p.m. ET on their expiration day
  Effective TBD (SR-CBOE-2025-011, GTH classes only): SPX AM would cease at 9:25 a.m. ET
    on the expiration date (usually a Friday); VIX AM at 9:00 a.m. ET (usually a Wednesday)
  a separate notice will be issued once an effective date is determined; do not treat TBD as operative
=== B. SOQ (published as SET) is not the prior close, official open, or a later spot ===
  Thursday close 5000
  Friday official index open (spot amalgam) 5005
  later Friday spot print 5010
  SOQ / SET (official opens of constituents) 5002
  AM-settled exercise settlement value is the SOQ, not the other three numbers
  SOQ is not calculated until all constituents have opened; it is not anchored to a time of day
  if a constituent does not open, its last trade price from the prior trading day is used in the SOQ
=== C. OCC cash-dividend adjustments (IM 54262 worked examples) ===
  ordinary cash dividends (regular policy or practice) do not adjust, regardless of size
  ordinary quarterly $2.00/share on a 100-share contract = $200.00 -> no adjustment
  example 1: $0.10 special on a 100-share option yields $10.00 -> no adjustment
    100-share value $10.00; adjust? False
  example 2: $0.10 special on 100-share and 150-share (prior 3-for-2 split)
    100-share value $10.00; 150-share value $15.00
    standard meets $12.50? False; 150-share adjusted? False
    the 150-share option is also not adjusted, because the standard-size contract does not meet the threshold
  example 3: $0.15 special on 100-share and 50-share (prior 1-for-2 reverse split)
    100-share value $15.00; 50-share value $7.50
    standard adjusted? True; 50-share adjusted? False
    the 50-share option is not adjusted ($7.50 < $12.50), even though the standard contract is
  the $12.50 test is per contract, not per share
  the issuer label 'special' is not binding; OCC decides case by case
  if adjusted: usually reduce the strike, or add cash to the deliverable; adjustments are made on the ex-date
  after corporate actions the deliverable may no longer be 100 shares; check the OCC information memo for a live event
  do not treat FINRA 11140(b) 25%+ ex-date deferral as an options-adjustment test
assertions passed: 8/8
disclaimer: learning only; not a settlement or adjustment engine; no product recommendation
